
 viewrqstusage - Report dsrqst request/file usage.

 Queries dsrqst-staged file requests stored in PostgreSQL database
 'rdadb' and produces a usage view/report grouped and filtered by the
 options you choose.

 USAGE:
   viewrqstusage [-C] ColumnNames [-O OrderColumnNames]
                 <one or more condition options>
                 [output and miscellaneous options]
                 [> OutputFile] [| lp -d PrinterName]

 BASIC RULES:

   1. -C ColumnNames is required (see COLUMN OPTIONS below).
      The '-C' flag may be omitted if ColumnNames is the first argument.

   2. At least one condition option must be given:
        -a -c -d -D -e -E -f -F -g -i -I -l -m -M -N -o -q -s -S -t -T -v -y

   3. Negation: for any condition option except -a, prepend '!' between
      the flag and value to invert the filter, e.g. '-o ! DSS'.

   4. Wildcards: condition options that take strings (-c, -e, -f, -g, -i,
      -l, -o, -S, -t) accept SQL wildcards '%' (any chars) and '_' (one char).

   5. By default the output is paginated with a header, footer, and
      column titles. Use -w for plain output (no header/totals).


 COLUMN OPTIONS:

   -C ColumnNames
        A string of one or more column letters listed below. The display
        order of columns matches their order in the string. At least one
        group column or summary column is required.

   -O OrderColumnNames
        Sort the output. Each letter must also appear in -C.
        UPPERCASE = ascending, lowercase = descending.

   Column letters:

     Group Columns:
       D* - DATE       - request date, YYYY-MM-DD (e.g. 2004-04-25)
       E* - EMAIL      - user email address
       G* - ORGNAME    - organization name
       I* - FIRSTNAME  - user first name
       K  - TIME       - time requested
       L* - LASTNAME   - user last name
       M* - MONTH      - YYYY-MM (e.g. 2004-04)
       N* - COUNTRY    - country code of the user
       O* - ORGTYPE    - organization type (DSS, NCAR, UNIV, OTHER)
       P* - PROCESSBY  - login name of the request-owning specialist
       Q* - QUARTER    - 1, 2, 3, or 4
       R  - RQSTNOTE   - request note for subset
       S  - FROM       - from-flag the request was initiated from
       T* - DATASET    - format dsnnn.n (e.g. d540001)
       U* - FILENAME   - WEB file name accessed
       V* - RINDEX     - request index
       W* - METHOD     - download method
       Y* - YEAR       - YYYY

       (*) = column may be displayed with zero usages when -z is used.

     Summary Columns:
       A - DSCOUNT    - number of datasets in the group
       B - MBYTERQST  - requested data size (MB) by the group
       C - #UNIQUSER  - number of unique users in the group
       F - MBINPUT    - input data size (MB) by the group
       H - #FILERQST  - number of files requested by the group
       J - #UNIQFILE  - number of unique files requested by the group
       Z - #REQUEST   - number of requests by the group

     Index Column:
       X - INDEX      - 1-based row index (use as the first column)


 CONDITION OPTIONS:

   -a   All recorded request usage since 2005-01-01.
   -A RowLimit                       Limit the number of rows returned.
   -c CountryCodes                   Users from these country codes.
   -d DateList                       Requests on these dates (YYYY-MM-DD).
   -D StartDate [EndDate]            Requests between two dates.
   -e EMailList                      Requests by users with these emails.
                                     Escape '@' in shell, e.g. 'zji\@ucar.edu'.
   -E StartDate [EndDate]            Requests by users notified of dataset
                                     updates between these dates.
   -f FileNameList                   Requests for these file names.
   -F MinFileName [MaxFileName]      File names in this range.
   -g OrgNames                       Users from these organization names.
   -h                                Pair with -e to include historical
                                     emails users registered with.
   -i FirstNameList                  Users with these first names.
   -I EmailIDList                    Requests by users for these email IDs.
   -l LastNameList                   Users with these last names.
   -m MonthList                      Requests in these months (YYYY-MM).
   -M RequestTypeList                Requests via these download methods.
   -N MinReads [MaxReads]            Groups with read counts in this range.
   -o OrgTypes                       Users from these org types.
                                     Default: '-o ! DSS' (excludes DSS).
                                     Use '-o ALL' to include every type.
   -q QuarterList                    Requests in these quarters (1-4).
   -s FromFlags                      Filter by from-flag value.
   -S SpecialistLoginNames           Specialists who own the requests.
   -t DatasetList                    Requests for these datasets.
   -T MinDataset [MaxDataset]        Requests for datasets in this ID range,
                                     e.g. '-T d540000 d550009'.
   -v RequestIndices                 Requests with these request indices.
   -y YearList                       Requests in these years (YYYY).


 OUTPUT AND MISCELLANEOUS OPTIONS:

   -H Title           Replace the default report title.
   -L Delimiter       Use Delimiter between columns instead of spaces.
   -U SizeUnit        Show sizes in unit: B, K, M, or G.
   -n                 Show requests submitted on the command line by NCAR
                      internal users.
   -w                 Simple format: no header, no totals.
   -z                 Include zero usages for the specified fields.
   > OutputFile       Redirect output to a file.
   | lp -d Printer    Send output to the named printer (e.g. lj100).


 EXAMPLES:

   View annual request usage in 2005 with columns INDEX, EMAIL, ORGTYPE,
   #FILERQST, MBYTERQST; sort by ORGTYPE ascending and MBYTERQST
   descending:

      viewrqstusage XEOHB -y 2005 -O Ob

   Restrict to files matching '/DSS/Y%':

      viewrqstusage XEOHB -y 2005 -f /DSS/Y% -O Ob

   Same, excluding DSS users, and save to a file:

      viewrqstusage XEOHB -y 2005 -f /DSS/Y% -o ! DSS -O Ob > rqstusage.out
